00:19:44,899 --> 00:19:50,220
I understand why somebody would do that- because they want this scouts to have some experience in that

223
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:53,260
Before they take on a full Eagle Scout project.

224
00:19:53,379 --> 00:19:58,140
But you can't do that because it's adding to the advancement requirements.

225
00:19:58,379 --> 00:20:00,580
So let's remember these things:

226
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:07,140
Service projects can be conducted individually or through participation in a troop or patrol project,

227
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:11,820
And there's no verbiage in anything that I have found that we can

228
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:18,740
Require scouts to participate in a given project to fulfill the requirement. It's totally up to them.

229
00:20:18,740 --> 00:20:26,380
There's nothing that indicates that all the hours must be earned in a single project. if the rank requirement says six hours,

230
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:34,340
It can be six or twelve different projects, or it can be one project, or it can be three projects, so long as the scout accrues

231
00:20:34,340 --> 00:20:37,740
The hours needed. participation is the only requirement.

232
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:42,420
They can be a part of the planning and development or leadership of these projects,

233
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:47,180
But they cannot be required to take part in the planning, development or leadership of the project

234
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:55,500
And we are encouraged to approve participation in another Scouts Eagle Scout service project for the rank requirement.

235
00:20:55,500 --> 00:21:01,140
Service to others, as I said before, is a key concept we hope to build in our scouts

236
00:21:01,140 --> 00:21:05,580
And the opportunity to do this is built into the requirements.

237
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:10,380
The few minutes we'll have in a discussion, helping them discover what service means,

238
00:21:10,380 --> 00:21:12,700
The nature of the service itself

239
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:18,300
And whether or not in their opinion- not our opinion, not our judgment, but in their opinion-

240
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:22,860
If that service qualifies towards the requirement, is important.

241
00:21:22,860 --> 00:21:27,620
And finally I'll say this: service is more than a requirement.

242
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:33,500
Service is more than just getting something for yourself so you can get your next rank.

243
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:37,140
Service is a habit. service is a way of life.

244
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:41,580
Looking after the interests of other people, helping other people at all times,

245
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:49,180
Being trustworthy, loyal, helpful, friendly, courteous, kind, obedient, cheerful, thrifty, brave, clean and reverent:

246
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:51,340
This is the way that we live our lives.

247
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:56,940
These are the things that are going to follow our Scouts into the rest of their lives,

248
00:21:56,940 --> 00:22:06,420
And we have the precious opportunity of helping them discover the joy of being of service to other people.

249
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:13,940
Don't overshadow that with jargon and judgment about fulfilling a rank requirement.

250
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:22,100
There shouldn't be any question in any unit out there that there are plenty of opportunities to fulfill those rank requirements

251
00:22:22,100 --> 00:22:30,900
Baked into the units program and certainly in encouraging the initiative of all our Scouts to live a life of service to others.

